<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paul von Lettow-Vorbeck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1870">1870</a>–<a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paul von Lettow-Vorbeck was a German general who commanded the defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-east-africa">German East Africa</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. With a small force of German and African askari troops he won the Battle of Tanga in 1914 and then waged a long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> campaign through Tanganyika, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a>. He surrendered only on 25 November 1918, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paul-von-lettow-vorbeck.jpg" alt="Paul von Lettow-Vorbeck" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photoatelier Hermann Noack, Berlin; cropped, retouched and resolution reduced by Jossi2 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_Paul_von_Lettow-Vorbeck_LCCN2014719610b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
